      "comment": "Nameless Bard: Fly, Fly Away",
      "content": "At the end of the Carmen Dei story quest, Venti says he first heard a song from his lost friend and recites four short lines: fly away like a bird in the sky; see the world on my behalf; may you fly to the heavens. The scene goes quiet. It is the only song of his that Venti quotes.",
